# What following the README *in this clone* leaves behind, rather than in a
# directory beside it. The quickstart says `feather init my_feature_store`, so
# the intended shape keeps all three out of the repository root; this is for
# the developer who runs the commands here instead.
#
# `feather.toml` is the one that matters rather than the tidiest. It has
# `password` and `secret` fields, the settings schema resolves them from
# `${ENV_VAR}` and the architecture doc calls a literal secret in this file a
# bug, but the field still accepts a literal. An unignored settings file is a
# credential one `git add -A` from being published, and it is the kind of file
# that gets created by running the quickstart, which is the first thing anyone
# does after cloning. Nothing here is needed by the test suite: no
# `feather.toml` is tracked, and the tests that read one build it under
# `tmp_path`.
feather.toml
definitions/
data/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.pytest_cache/
